# (1) Console Warnings in Grid2/Grid Component

## New file: `deleteLegacyGridProps.ts`

**Imports:**
```ts
import { Breakpoint, Breakpoints } from '../createTheme';
```

**Warning message generator:**
```ts
const getLegacyGridWarning = (propName: 'item' | 'zeroMinWidth' | Breakpoint) => {
  if (['item', 'zeroMinWidth'].includes(propName)) {
    return `The \`${propName}\` prop has been removed and is no longer necessary. You can safely remove it.`;
  }
  // #host-reference
  return `The \`${propName}\` prop has been removed. See https://mui.com/material-ui/migration/upgrade-to-grid-v2/ for migration instructions.`;
};
```

**Once-per-session mechanism** uses a module-level array tracking already-warned props:
```ts
const warnedAboutProps: string[] = [];
```

The main function deletes each legacy prop and collects names to warn about:
- Checks `props.item !== undefined`, deletes it, pushes `'item'`
- Checks `props.zeroMinWidth !== undefined`, deletes it, pushes `'zeroMinWidth'`
- Iterates `breakpoints.keys`, deleting any defined breakpoint prop and pushing its name

The warning loop only runs outside production and only warns once per prop:
```ts
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') {
    propsToWarn.forEach((prop) => {
      if (!warnedAboutProps.includes(prop)) {
        warnedAboutProps.push(prop);
        console.warn(`MUI Grid2: ${getLegacyGridWarning(prop)}\n`);
      }
    });
  }
```

